    "q-163119": {
      "dom_id": "step-q163119",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the plane $x=-2,$ the surface $x={z}^{2}+y,$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,-2\\le x\\le {z}^{2}+y\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{{z}^{2}+y}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=-2}^{x={z}^{2}+y}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{2}+y-(-2)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{z}^{2}+y+2\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}+(y+2)z]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{3}+y+2\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7}{3}+y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{3}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot 2+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {2}^{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-163119-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{20}{3}",
